Q8. Explain the different types of CSS with examples.

1. Inline CSS: CSS is written inside the HTML element using the style attribute.
Example: <p style="color: red;">Hello</p>

2. Internal CSS: CSS is written inside a <style> tag in the HTML head section.
Example:
<style>
  p { color: blue; }
</style>

3. External CSS: CSS is written in a separate .css file and connected using a link tag.
Example in HTML: <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
Example in style.css: p { color: green; }

Q9. Differentiate between HTML, CSS and JavaScript.

HTML: It gives structure to a webpage, such as headings, paragraphs, images and buttons.
CSS: It gives style to a webpage, such as colors, fonts, spacing and layout.
JavaScript: It adds actions and interactivity, such as button clicks and form validation.

In simple words: HTML is the structure, CSS is the design and JavaScript is the behaviour.

Q10. Short answers.

a. What is the role of Bootstrap in web development?
Bootstrap is a CSS framework that helps developers create responsive and mobile-friendly websites using ready-made classes and components.

b. What is jQuery and why was it widely used?
jQuery is a JavaScript library that makes HTML selection, event handling, animations and AJAX easier with shorter code. It was widely used because it simplified JavaScript and browser differences.

c. What is React.js and what problem does it solve?
React.js is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces. It helps developers create reusable components and update webpage content efficiently.
